        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Pay for the tier that matches your route.</strong> Curbside is
            fine for a light machine on a level route with two helpers. Anything involving stairs,
            a single person or an apartment building usually justifies room of choice, and white
            glove is often the best value if you would rather not
            <a href="/how-to-assemble-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">assemble it yourself</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Settle the building rules, measure the route for the crate, and on the day
            <strong class="text-white">inspect before you sign</strong>: photograph the box, write
            specific damage on the receipt, and keep the packaging until the machine has run. If
            you are moving it yourself, our
            <a href="/how-to-move-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">moving guide</a>
